    "text": "Let G be a group of automorphisms of an abelian group of prime exponent.\nSuppose that there exists x ∈ G such that x is regular of order 3 and the order of\n[x, g] is finite for every g ∈ G. Is it true that ⟨xG ⟩ is locally finite? V. D. Mazurov",
